<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Home-screen "Frequency Cassette" widget (renamed 2026-09-10, direct user request — was
     "Soundtrack") — plays the app's own ambient "Log Screen" music tracks (the same 4
     choices as Profile > Display > Sound > Ambient Music: 1.0/2.0/3.0 Login Screen +
     Convene) via SoundtrackPlaybackService, a genuine foreground MediaPlayer service so
     playback survives the widget/app not being on screen.

     Restyled to use the user's own product photo (public/widgets/cassette-widget.png,
     alpha-cutout around the device's own irregular silhouette, decoded by
     SoundtrackWidget.java) rather than a hand-drawn reinterpretation — see that class's own
     header for why decodeAsset + this file's scaleType="fitXY" (not fitCenter/centerCrop) is
     required for the fractional overlay positions below to track the photo's real button
     positions at any widget size.

     Track name text and the transport controls are positioned as FRACTIONS of the photo's
     own measured pixel layout (currently a 1858×1017 source: the blank cream panel inside
     the tape-reel window at x 725-1580/y 417-519 for text; the 4 physical button labels at
     x 613-1552/y 824-957 for controls; the yellow diagram panel at roughly x 204-501/
     y 224-596 for the shuffle toggle), built from nested weighted LinearLayouts (RemoteViews
     has no percentage-margin attribute, so weight-sum spacers are the standard substitute).
     Re-measured and the button mapping corrected 2026-09-10 per direct user review of a
     debug overlay image (see PHASE/commit history — this is the SECOND numeric pass; the
     first pass's positions were confirmed accurate by the same overlay method, but its
     button-to-action mapping was wrong) — the real mapping, left to right on the 4 physical
     buttons: Prev, Next, Loop, Play/Stop. Shuffle didn't fit anywhere in that row and was
     moved into the middle of the yellow diagram panel on the left instead, per the user's
     own direction.

     Icon rendering fix (same day, direct user report of "glitched or invisible" button
     icons): every control below except Play/Stop now renders NO icon at all — just an
     invisible tap zone over the photo's own already-printed button face, plus the existing
     selected-overlay tint for Loop/Shuffle's on/off state. Root cause: a button's weighted
     cell height is a FRACTION OF THE WIDGET'S OWN HEIGHT (~13% for the button row), and
     since home-screen widgets are typically wide-and-short (e.g. a 3×2-cell placement is
     roughly 250×110dp), that fraction can collapse to under 15dp tall — an icon with
     scaleType="fitCenter" inside a cell that short scales down to near-nothing, which is
     what "invisible" was. Play/Stop is the one control that genuinely needs a live icon (it
     has to show playing vs paused, which the static photo can't), so it keeps one — but
     wrapped in its own FIXED-size inner box (22dp square, gravity="center") instead of
     filling the outer weighted cell directly, so its aspect ratio can never collapse no
     matter how short that outer cell gets.

     The root background is genuinely transparent (@android:color/transparent) — the photo's
     own alpha cutout is the widget's real visible edge.

     TWO alternate content blocks — widget_soundtrack_content_normal (the photo-mapped
     layout above) reads fine down to 2 cells tall, but doesn't fit in a 1-cell-tall
     placement at all (the photo would be squeezed into an unrecognizable sliver);
     widget_soundtrack_content_compact falls back to a plain flat row — text + small FIXED-dp
     icon buttons (not weighted, so they don't have this same squish problem at all) — which
     SoundtrackWidget.java switches to below its own height threshold, same compact-mode
     pattern PulseBannerWidget.java already uses. Both blocks' data/PendingIntents are
     applied identically every render; only whichever one is actually visible matters.

     No plain <View> anywhere (RemoteViews' allowlist doesn't include it) — spacer/positioner
     layers use empty FrameLayouts instead. -->
<FrameLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:background="@android:color/transparent">

    <ImageView
        android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_bg_art"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="match_parent"
        android:scaleType="fitXY"
        android:contentDescription="@null" />

    <!-- ═══ Normal (>= 2 cells tall): photo-position-mapped overlay ═══ -->
    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_content_normal"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="match_parent"
        android:orientation="vertical">

        <!-- Row 1/3 (vertical weights 41/10/49 ≈ photo's y 417-519 of 1017) — track name,
             centered in the cream panel inside the tape-reel window. Tap to cycle to the
             next track, same interaction as the Calculator widget's own copy-target pill. -->
        <FrameLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="41" />
        <LinearLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="10"
            android:orientation="horizontal">
            <FrameLayout
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="39" />
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_track_name"
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="45"
                android:gravity="center">
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_track_name_text"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:textColor="#3D2817"
                    android:textSize="14sp"
                    android:textStyle="bold"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:ellipsize="end" />
            </LinearLayout>
            <FrameLayout
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="16" />
        </LinearLayout>
        <FrameLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="49" />

        <!-- Row 2/3 (vertical weights 81/13/6 ≈ photo's y 824-957 of 1017) — the 4 real
             physical button labels, horizontal weights 33/11/12/14/13/17 ≈ their real x
             613/819/1047/1311/1552 of 1858. Left to right: Prev, Next, Loop, Play/Stop. -->
        <FrameLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="81" />
        <LinearLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="13"
            android:orientation="horizontal">
            <FrameLayout
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="33" />
            <!-- No icon — see file header ("Icon rendering fix"). Just an invisible tap zone
                 over the photo's own printed button face. -->
            <ImageButton
                android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_prev"
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="11"
                android:background="@android:color/transparent"
                android:contentDescription="@string/widget_soundtrack_prev_aria" />
            <ImageButton
                android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_next"
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="12"
                android:background="@android:color/transparent"
                android:contentDescription="@string/widget_soundtrack_next_aria" />
            <!-- Loop toggle. Selected-state overlay: RemoteViews can't runtime-swap a view's
                 own background, so the "on" highlight is a second view toggled by visibility
                 — that overlay tint is this button's only on/off indicator now (no icon). -->
            <FrameLayout
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="14">
                <FrameLayout
                    android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_loop_selected"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="match_parent"
                    android:background="@drawable/widget_target_selected_emerald"
                    android:visibility="gone" />
                <ImageButton
                    android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_loop"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="match_parent"
                    android:background="@android:color/transparent"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/widget_soundtrack_loop_aria" />
            </FrameLayout>
            <!-- Play/Stop — the one control that needs a REAL icon (has to show playing vs
                 paused; the static photo can't). Icon lives in a FIXED 22dp square centered
                 inside the outer weighted cell, not filling it directly, so it can never be
                 squashed by that cell's own aspect ratio the way a fitCenter-filled icon in a
                 short weighted cell was (see file header). -->
            <FrameLayout
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="13">
                <ImageButton
                    android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_play"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="match_parent"
                    android:background="@android:color/transparent"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/widget_soundtrack_play_aria" />
                <ImageView
                    android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_play_icon"
                    android:layout_width="22dp"
                    android:layout_height="22dp"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:src="@android:drawable/ic_media_play"
                    android:tint="#3D2817"
                    android:contentDescription="@null" />
            </FrameLayout>
            <FrameLayout
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="17" />
        </LinearLayout>
        <FrameLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="6" />
    </LinearLayout>

    <!-- Shuffle toggle, moved into the middle of the yellow diagram panel on the left
         (horizontal weights 11/16/73 ≈ x 204-501 of 1858; vertical weights 22/37/41 ≈
         y 224-596 of 1017) — per direct user direction (it didn't fit in the 4-button row).
         A SIBLING of widget_soundtrack_content_normal (not nested inside it) since it needs
         its own independent weighted-positioner tree rooted at the full widget height rather
         than the transport row's — SoundtrackWidget.java toggles this id's visibility in
         lockstep with content_normal/content_compact so it doesn't float over the compact
         layout too. No icon, same reasoning as Prev/Next/Loop above — the selected-overlay
         tint is its only on/off indicator. -->
    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_shuffle_dial_wrap"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="match_parent"
        android:orientation="vertical">
        <FrameLayout android:layout_width="match_parent" android:layout_height="0dp" android:layout_weight="22" />
        <LinearLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="37"
            android:orientation="horizontal">
            <FrameLayout android:layout_width="0dp" android:layout_height="match_parent" android:layout_weight="11" />
            <FrameLayout
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="16">
                <FrameLayout
                    android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_shuffle_selected"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="match_parent"
                    android:background="@drawable/widget_target_selected_emerald"
                    android:visibility="gone" />
                <ImageButton
                    android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_shuffle"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="match_parent"
                    android:background="@android:color/transparent"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/widget_soundtrack_shuffle_aria" />
            </FrameLayout>
            <FrameLayout android:layout_width="0dp" android:layout_height="match_parent" android:layout_weight="73" />
        </LinearLayout>
        <FrameLayout android:layout_width="match_parent" android:layout_height="0dp" android:layout_weight="41" />
    </LinearLayout>

    <!-- ═══ Compact (1 cell tall): plain flat row, FIXED-dp icon buttons (no weighted-cell
         squish problem at all — kept as normal icons here) ═══ -->
    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_content_compact"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="match_parent"
        android:orientation="horizontal"
        android:gravity="center_vertical"
        android:paddingLeft="8dp"
        android:paddingRight="8dp"
        android:visibility="gone">

        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_track_name_compact_text"
            android:layout_width="0dp"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_weight="1"
            android:layout_marginRight="6dp"
            android:textColor="#3D2817"
            android:textSize="16sp"
            android:textStyle="bold"
            android:maxLines="1"
            android:ellipsize="end" />

        <FrameLayout
            android:layout_width="24dp"
            android:layout_height="24dp">
            <FrameLayout
                android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_shuffle_selected_compact"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:background="@drawable/widget_target_selected_emerald"
                android:visibility="gone" />
            <ImageButton
                android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_shuffle_compact"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:background="@android:color/transparent"
                android:src="@drawable/ic_shuffle_widget"
                android:scaleType="fitCenter"
                android:padding="2dp"
                android:contentDescription="@string/widget_soundtrack_shuffle_aria" />
        </FrameLayout>

        <ImageButton
            android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_prev_compact"
            android:layout_width="24dp"
            android:layout_height="24dp"
            android:layout_marginLeft="6dp"
            android:background="@android:color/transparent"
            android:src="@android:drawable/ic_media_previous"
            android:tint="#3D2817"
            android:scaleType="fitCenter"
            android:contentDescription="@string/widget_soundtrack_prev_aria" />

        <ImageButton
            android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_play_compact"
            android:layout_width="32dp"
            android:layout_height="32dp"
            android:layout_marginLeft="6dp"
            android:background="@android:color/transparent"
            android:src="@android:drawable/ic_media_play"
            android:tint="#3D2817"
            android:scaleType="fitCenter"
            android:padding="4dp"
            android:contentDescription="@string/widget_soundtrack_play_aria" />

        <ImageButton
            android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_next_compact"
            android:layout_width="24dp"
            android:layout_height="24dp"
            android:layout_marginLeft="6dp"
            android:background="@android:color/transparent"
            android:src="@android:drawable/ic_media_next"
            android:tint="#3D2817"
            android:scaleType="fitCenter"
            android:contentDescription="@string/widget_soundtrack_next_aria" />

        <FrameLayout
            android:layout_width="24dp"
            android:layout_height="24dp"
            android:layout_marginLeft="6dp">
            <FrameLayout
                android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_loop_selected_compact"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:background="@drawable/widget_target_selected_emerald"
                android:visibility="gone" />
            <ImageButton
                android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_loop_compact"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:background="@android:color/transparent"
                android:src="@drawable/ic_loop_widget"
                android:scaleType="fitCenter"
                android:padding="2dp"
                android:contentDescription="@string/widget_soundtrack_loop_aria" />
        </FrameLayout>
    </LinearLayout>
</FrameLayout>
